<BaseLayout title="About Wanda" description="About Wanda and the ideas behind this personal research journal.">
  <header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">A NOTE FROM THE AUTHOR</p><h1>About</h1><p>A place to think carefully, explain clearly, and share what I learn.</p></header>
  <article class="about-copy">
    <p class="about-lead">Hello, I'm Wanda.</p>
    <p>I'm a researcher working around neutral-atom quantum technologies, with interests spanning atomic physics, quantum control, and scientific computing.</p>
    <p>This journal is where I make room for two kinds of writing. The first is explanatory: taking a physical idea that may seem specialised and making its logic accessible without removing the science. The second is research-oriented: documenting methods, interpreting papers, and reflecting on the questions that emerge while building and studying quantum systems.</p>
    <p>Some articles are written for readers encountering a topic for the first time; others assume familiarity with the field. Each piece will make its intended level clear.</p>
    <p>The views and explanations here are my own and are not official statements from any institution or employer. Research details will be shared with care, respecting publication status, collaboration agreements, and intellectual-property obligations.</p>
    <div class="about-signoff">Wanda<br/><span>Quantum physics · Research · Ideas</span></div>
    <p class="about-contact">Find me on <a href="https://github.com/wanda0929" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
